# Native Codex dispatch

Native workers require verified dispatch capability: discovery, configured model,
sandbox enforcement, thread status/resume. Catalog checks do not establish them.
Missing capability blocks, never silently substitutes OpenCode or widens sandbox.

Spawn the project planner for planning; builder remains the default implementer.
codex-dev requires explicit per-task choice. Native reviewer/fallback/tester use
their pinned project agents. Keep Codex planner/implementer/reviewer/tester thread
ids in separate typed role rows; new task/role/model starts
fresh. Spawn review from file-based brief without inheriting/forking author chat.
Two OpenAI-family models are not independent review; resolve actual served family.

Each attempt gets an unused prompt pass and Artifacts link. Export a transcript
only when runtime supports it; otherwise record unavailable plus actual thread id.
Native read-only reviewers return full verdict/findings: lead records unchanged
in Review verdicts, sets Latest handoff, then runs verify-state. Testers record
their own results; workspace-write does not enforce their narrower test/state-only
scope, so check the diff for out-of-scope edits.

Use host completion notifications. Never send a second writer into an active
thread. After interruption inspect actual status/task first; unknown activity
blocks resume/replacement. If resume is lost, record loss and start from the task
only after confirming inactivity. No sandbox escalation or approval bypass;
OpenCode auto consent does not grant native permission changes.

For exact team lead capture/resume, only when the launcher extra is installed,
use .agent-pipeline/bin/codex-lead.sh and normally trusted, explicitly merged capture hooks.
Never choose latest conversation or replace a captured lead pin with a worker.
